  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-dimidiata",
      "html": "<ul><li>One of two species in the Betta dimidiata complex.</li><li>IUCN Red List: Vulnerable.</li><li>F1 (first generation from wild-caught bettas).</li><li>Max size: 2.3 inches.</li><li>Breeding: mouthbrooder.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-dimidiata",
      "html": "<p>This betta is found in the West Kalimantan area of Indonesia.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-dimidiata",
      "html": "<ul><li>TDS: 60 - 200 (kept in soft water with low TDS to match other wild bettas, but they are more tolerant of water conditions.)</li><li>pH: 5.0 - 7.0</li><li>Temperature: 75-85°F (much better coloration at warmer temperatures above 78°F)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-dimidiata",
      "html": "<p>Carnivorous. We currently feed them live blackworms, frozen bloodworms and pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-dimidiata",
      "html": "<p>Fairly peaceful and can be kept in groups. Males will show off and flare at each other from time to time but no real harm is done. We recommend a pair per 5 gallon tank.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-dimidiata",
      "html": "<p>Dark gray/brown body with long flowing fins. A translucent blue edge can be seen on the fins, more pronounced on the anal fin.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-dimidiata",
      "html": "<p>Mouthbrooder.</p>"
    }
  ],
